德怀特告诉迈克尔，这种行为会让他的工作变得多余。

1099
00:46:40.660 --> 00:46:45.040
Like, if people can just go around Michael straight to corporate, then what is Michael's job, really?
如果人们都能绕过迈克尔直接找公司高层，那迈克尔的工作到底还有什么意义？

1100
00:46:45.420 --> 00:46:48.240
This is going to make Michael spiral out.
这会让迈克尔彻底失控的。

1101
00:46:49.080 --> 00:46:55.700
Meanwhile, Kevin is going to walk up to Danny Cordray at the water cooler, and he's going to smack him on the butt.
与此同时，凯文会走到饮水机旁找丹尼·科德雷，然后拍他的屁股。

1102
00:46:55.880 --> 00:46:56.800
Did you catch that?
你注意到了吗？

1103
00:46:56.960 --> 00:46:57.400
I did.
我注意到了。

1104
00:46:57.500 --> 00:46:58.860
That's how he gets his attention.
那是他引起对方注意的方式。

1105
00:46:59.160 --> 00:46:59.980
Yeah, I did.
没错，我注意到了。

1106
00:46:59.980 --> 00:47:05.940
And I also caught Timothy Oliphant as Danny looking back at him like, what's happening?
我还看到蒂莫西·奥利芬特饰演的丹尼回头看他，那表情仿佛在说：这什么情况？

1107
00:47:06.220 --> 00:47:07.120
What are you doing?
你在干什么？

1108
00:47:07.880 --> 00:47:17.560
They need his attention because Andy and Kevin are going to explain that as much as they would like to come to public school for this party, they're going to bow out.
他们需要引起他的注意，因为安迪和凯文要解释说，尽管他们很想去公立学校参加这个派对，但他们决定不去了。

1109
00:47:17.860 --> 00:47:21.400
Because Jim and Pam asked them not to go, is what they say.
他们说是吉姆和帕姆让他们别去的。

1110
00:47:21.920 --> 00:47:26.860
Danny's going to talk to Jim and Pam, but Kevin's like, don't say me and Andy talked to you.
丹尼会去找吉姆和帕姆谈，但凯文却说：别说是我和安迪找过你。

1111
00:47:27.220 --> 00:47:28.500
Or we'll kill you.
不然我们就杀了你。

1112
00:47:28.580 --> 00:47:29.440
Or you'll be dead.
或者说你会没命的。

1113
00:47:29.440 --> 00:47:31.680
Yeah, I mean, what is going on?
是啊，我是说，这到底是怎么回事？

1114
00:47:33.380 --> 00:47:36.120
Kelly is going to arrive back to work in a new costume.
凯莉会换上一套新装扮回到公司。

1115
00:47:37.000 --> 00:47:38.480
It's very elaborate.
非常精致复杂。

1116
00:47:38.480 --> 00:47:40.920
I looked in the shooting draft, and here's what it said.
我查了拍摄剧本，上面是这么写的。

1117
00:47:41.400 --> 00:47:43.560
Kelly walks in with some shopping bags.
凯莉提着几个购物袋走进来。

1118
00:47:43.760 --> 00:47:46.540
She is an elaborate, sexy clown.
她打扮成了一个精致、性感的小丑。

1119
00:47:47.440 --> 00:47:48.740
That's what it is.
就是这样。

1120
00:47:49.240 --> 00:47:50.220
I wondered.
我还在纳闷呢。

1121
00:47:50.480 --> 00:47:54.640
I thought maybe she was being a pop star from a music video or something.
我以为她是在模仿某个音乐录影带里的流行歌星之类的。

1122
00:47:54.920 --> 00:47:56.860
She's an elaborate, sexy clown.
她是个精致、性感的小丑。

1123
00:47:56.980 --> 00:47:57.240
Okay.
好吧。

1124
00:47:57.240 --> 00:48:00.980
She also shares about how much she spent on this costume.
她还分享了自己在服装上花了多少钱。

1125
00:48:00.980 --> 00:48:02.160
It's in deleted scenes.
这在删减片段里。

1126
00:48:02.360 --> 00:48:02.880
Let's hear it.
让我们听听看。

1127
00:48:03.680 --> 00:48:05.300
My costume cost $600.
我的服装花了600美元。

1128
00:48:05.840 --> 00:48:11.480
If I had the coupon book, it would have cost 20% less than that, which is why I need that coupon book.
如果我有优惠券手册，就能便宜20%，所以我才需要那本优惠券手册。

1129
00:48:12.200 --> 00:48:13.920
By the way, we have another coupon.
顺便说一下，我们还有一张优惠券。

1130
00:48:14.880 --> 00:48:16.500
No one has said coupon.
还没人说过优惠券这个词。

1131
00:48:17.180 --> 00:48:18.960
Well, now Angela is peeved.
好吧，现在安吉拉生气了。

1132
00:48:19.100 --> 00:48:22.040
She says, Kelly, you cannot change costumes in the middle of the day.
她说：凯莉，你不能在一天中间换装。

1133
00:48:22.200 --> 00:48:23.060
Pam, she's out.
帕姆，她出局了。

1134
00:48:23.400 --> 00:48:26.180
This leads to a back and forth where Oscar jumps in.
这引发了一场争论，奥斯卡也插了进来。

1135
00:48:26.360 --> 00:48:28.780
I want you guys to know I improvised the line.
我想让你们知道，那句台词是我即兴发挥的。

1136
00:48:29.100 --> 00:48:30.400
Yeah, shut it, Oscar.
是啊，闭嘴吧，奥斯卡。

1137
00:48:30.820 --> 00:48:31.100
Pam?
帕姆？

1138
00:48:31.740 --> 00:48:32.180
Nice.
不错。

1139
00:48:32.180 --> 00:48:38.900
And I also wanted to share with you guys, we could not get through my talking head in this penguin costume.
我还想和你们分享一下，我穿着这身企鹅装根本没法顺利完成我的单人访谈。

1140
00:48:39.080 --> 00:48:40.720
I can see why.
我能理解为什么。

1141
00:48:40.960 --> 00:48:42.260
It's so funny.
太搞笑了。

1142
00:48:42.500 --> 00:48:44.440
You're such an angry penguin.
你是一只如此愤怒的企鹅。

1143
00:48:44.440 --> 00:48:45.400
You're so mad.
你太生气了。

1144
00:48:45.680 --> 00:48:54.260
The penguin costume was so incredibly comfortable, but the way the beak went up and over my forehead kind of limited my side vision.
这件企鹅装穿起来极其舒服，但喙部向上延伸盖住额头的方式限制了我的侧向视野。

1145
00:48:54.260 --> 00:49:00.640
So even when I turn to you, when I say shut it, Oscar, Pam, if you look at how I turn, it looks like I have a crick in my neck,
所以即使我转向你们说“闭嘴吧，奥斯卡，帕姆”，如果你看我转头的方式，看起来就像我脖子落枕了一样，

1146
00:49:00.660 --> 00:49:04.320
but it's just the way the penguin head set on my forehead.
但那只是企鹅头套戴在我额头上的方式导致的。

1147
00:49:05.600 --> 00:49:10.560
Anyway, Dean and I were cracking up so much in this talking head, I kind of felt like we had to hear it.
总之，迪恩和我在拍这段单人访谈时笑得前仰后合，我觉得我们得听听看。

1148
00:49:10.840 --> 00:49:11.200
Yay!
耶！

1149
00:49:12.640 --> 00:49:13.980
This is an amazing prize.
这真是个了不起的奖品。

1150
00:49:14.280 --> 00:49:19.440
I mean, I don't even want to give Pam a compliment because she's so ugh, but she did a good job.
我是说，我甚至不想夸帕姆，因为她太让人无语了，但她确实做得不错。

1151
00:49:19.920 --> 00:49:21.240
I really want that coupon book.
我真的很想要那本优惠券手册。

1152
00:49:21.240 --> 00:49:24.140
I love when you're like the blech.
我喜欢你那种“呕”的样子。

1153
00:49:24.260 --> 00:49:25.200
She's so blech.
她真是太让人倒胃口了。

1154
00:49:26.880 --> 00:49:28.940
That was so much fun to do.
那次真的太好玩了。

1155
00:49:29.320 --> 00:49:31.380
I loved that penguin costume.
我超爱那套企鹅装。

1156
00:49:31.380 --> 00:49:33.360
It was like wearing pajamas all day.
穿起来就像整天穿着睡衣一样。

1157
00:49:33.580 --> 00:49:36.860
Minus the way the head fit, everything else was awesome.
除了头套不太合身，其他地方都棒极了。

1158
00:49:38.710 --> 00:49:42.430
Well, next up, Dwight is, what is he doing?
好了，接下来，德怀特在干嘛？

1159
00:49:42.650 --> 00:49:44.470
He's throwing magnets away.
他在扔磁铁。

1160
00:49:44.710 --> 00:49:45.610
In the trash.
扔进垃圾桶里。

1161
00:49:45.610 --> 00:49:48.870
He doesn't like magnets that are too busy, that have too much going on.
他不喜欢那些花哨、设计太复杂的磁铁。

1162
00:49:48.990 --> 00:49:50.590
Yeah, they're interesting enough.
是啊，它们本身就够有意思了。

1163
00:49:50.590 --> 00:49:52.890
You don't have to tart them up with some design.
没必要非得加些花里胡哨的设计。

1164
00:49:53.450 --> 00:49:57.950
At 10 minutes, 33 seconds, I'd like to point out a personal Halloween decoration.
在10分33秒的时候，我想指出一个私人的万圣节装饰。

1165
00:49:58.470 --> 00:49:58.990
What?
什么？

1166
00:49:59.250 --> 00:50:03.130
I have the same spooky spider that's hanging over the table in the kitchen.
我也有那个挂在厨房桌子上的恐怖蜘蛛。

1167
00:50:03.130 --> 00:50:04.890
I decorate with it every Halloween.
我每年万圣节都会用它来装饰。

1168
00:50:05.690 --> 00:50:06.510
Spooky spider.
恐怖蜘蛛。

1169
00:50:06.510 --> 00:50:11.130
Michael is watching a conversation between Kevin and Gabe.
迈克尔正在看凯文和盖博的谈话。

1170
00:50:11.410 --> 00:50:14.930
It's pretty animated, and Michael is just freaking out.
谈话很激烈，迈克尔简直要疯了。

1171
00:50:15.070 --> 00:50:18.990
He thinks everyone is going over his head, around his head.
他觉得大家都在越过他，绕过他搞小动作。

1172
00:50:19.250 --> 00:50:20.770
What did he also say?
他还说了什么？

1173
00:50:20.990 --> 00:50:23.410
What do you call when someone takes you from the back?
当有人从背后搞你时，那叫什么？

1174
00:50:23.530 --> 00:50:24.350
And Dwight's like, no, no, no.
德怀特说，不，不，不。

1175
00:50:24.490 --> 00:50:24.770
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

1176
00:50:24.910 --> 00:50:25.410
What is it?
是什么来着？

1177
00:50:25.530 --> 00:50:27.150
Let's take them from behind.
让我们从背后搞定他们。

1178
00:50:27.630 --> 00:50:27.710
Yeah.
没错。

1179
00:50:28.390 --> 00:50:31.490
Michael thinks everyone's going to Gabe behind his back.
迈克尔以为大家都在背着他找盖博。

1180
00:50:31.790 --> 00:50:36.670
So he storms in to this conversation and really lays into Kevin.
所以他冲进谈话现场，狠狠地训斥了凯文。

1181
00:50:37.010 --> 00:50:39.950
Kevin is so upset and apologetic.
凯文非常难过，一直在道歉。

1182
00:50:40.190 --> 00:50:43.490
Shout out to Brian Baumgartner, who crushed this moment.
向布莱恩·鲍姆加特纳致敬，他把这一刻演绝了。

1183
00:50:43.630 --> 00:50:44.130
I agree.
我同意。

1184
00:50:44.650 --> 00:50:45.890
Such a good performance.
表演得太好了。

1185
00:50:46.050 --> 00:50:46.490
So good.
真的太棒了。

1186
00:50:46.650 --> 00:50:51.330
It turns out that he was just suggesting some Lady Gaga moves.
结果他只是在建议一些Lady Gaga的舞蹈动作。

1187
00:50:51.510 --> 00:50:53.970
But in the future, he'll tell Michael firSt.
但以后，他会先告诉迈克尔。

1188
00:50:54.330 --> 00:50:54.630
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1189
00:50:54.630 --> 00:50:57.410
There's a really great robot move he was going to show him.
他本来还想给他展示一个非常棒的机器人舞步。

1190
00:50:58.270 --> 00:51:00.950
And Michael's like, just don't let it happen again.
迈克尔说，别再有下次了。

1191
00:51:01.170 --> 00:51:04.570
And Kevin is like, no way, Jose.
凯文说，没门，何塞。

1192
00:51:05.170 --> 00:51:05.650
Yeah.
是啊。

1193
00:51:06.930 --> 00:51:08.650
I did look in the shooting draft.
我查了拍摄剧本。

1194
00:51:08.870 --> 00:51:10.510
The f*** you, Gabe, was not in the script.
那句“去你的，盖博”并不在剧本里。

1195
00:51:10.750 --> 00:51:12.790
I suspected it was not.
我猜就不在。

1196
00:51:12.790 --> 00:51:16.810
And the reason why is because they cut out of that so faSt.
原因就是他们切掉镜头的速度太快了。

1197
00:51:16.890 --> 00:51:17.130
Yeah.
没错。

1198
00:51:17.290 --> 00:51:19.570
Because I'm sure everyone cracked up after he did it.
因为我敢肯定他演完之后大家都笑喷了。

1199
00:51:19.710 --> 00:51:19.870
Yep.
没错。

1200
00:51:20.290 --> 00:51:23.870
Next up, we're in the conference room with Danny, Jim, and Pam.
接下来，我们在会议室里，有丹尼、吉姆和帕姆。

1201
00:51:23.870 --> 00:51:30.730
And they're just having a big laugh over this crazy notion that Jim and Pam wouldn't want people to go to his party.
他们正因为吉姆和帕姆不想让人去参加他的派对这种疯狂的想法而大笑不止。

1202
00:51:31.370 --> 00:51:33.410
Jenna, you are so great in this scene.
珍娜，你在这场戏里演得太棒了。

1203
00:51:33.770 --> 00:51:35.430
You are so good in it.
你演得真好。

1204
00:51:35.550 --> 00:51:37.070
I rewatched it a few times.
我重看了好几次。

1205
00:51:37.070 --> 00:51:38.870
I even recorded it.
我甚至把它录了下来。

1206
00:51:39.210 --> 00:51:44.230
When you say, no, actually, it was two dates.
当你回答说，不，其实那是两次约会。

1207
00:51:44.370 --> 00:51:45.410
We had a plan for a third.
我们本来计划有第三次的。

1208
00:51:45.570 --> 00:51:46.410
We have to hear it.
我们必须得听听。

1209
00:51:46.550 --> 00:51:47.250
It's too good.
这太棒了。

1210
00:51:49.060 --> 00:51:49.880
Was it too late?
是不是太晚了？

1211
00:51:49.880 --> 00:52:11.120
I think you and I do this in real life sometimes when things are awkward.
我觉得你和我现实生活中遇到尴尬情况时也会这样。

1212
00:52:11.120 --> 00:52:14.220
We go, well, somebody didn't bring their homework today.
我们会说，好吧，看来今天有人没带作业。

1213
00:52:14.580 --> 00:52:15.580
Yes, exactly.
没错，就是这样。

1214
00:52:16.020 --> 00:52:18.120
It's like, uh-oh, I feel uncomfortable.
就像是，噢噢，我觉得不舒服了。

1215
00:52:18.880 --> 00:52:21.040
I guess I shouldn't have backed into your car.
我想我不该倒车撞到你的车。

1216
00:52:21.240 --> 00:52:22.180
Ba-dee, ba-dee, burp.
吧唧，吧唧，嗝。

1217
00:52:24.840 --> 00:52:31.200
It was not in the shooting draft stage direction for you to be sing-songy or do any of that.
剧本的舞台说明里并没有要求你用这种唱歌般的语调或做任何类似动作。

1218
00:52:31.200 --> 00:52:34.600
But that was all your choice, and I thought it was fantastic.
但那完全是你自己的选择，我觉得太精彩了。

1219
00:52:34.940 --> 00:52:36.140
Aw, thank you, lady.
噢，谢谢你，女士。

1220
00:52:36.560 --> 00:52:38.460
Yeah, well, there's one other time I love.
是啊，还有另一个时刻我也很喜欢。

1221
00:52:38.540 --> 00:52:39.360
I'll bring it up later.
我稍后再提。

1222
00:52:39.760 --> 00:52:40.660
You're so good.
你太棒了。

1223
00:52:40.660 --> 00:52:42.120
You're so good in this episode.
你在这一集里演得真好。

1224
00:52:42.360 --> 00:52:43.360
I really loved it.
我真的很喜欢。

1225
00:52:43.440 --> 00:52:48.600
I have to say, I found Pam absolutely adorable in this episode, and I'm very, very proud of my performance.
我不得不说，我觉得帕姆在这一集里简直可爱极了，我为自己的表演感到非常、非常自豪。

1226
00:52:49.440 --> 00:52:52.060
If I could toot my own horn for a moment.
如果我能自夸一下的话。

1227
00:52:52.280 --> 00:52:53.940
And I'll use a voice to do it.
而且我要用一种特别的语调来说。

1228
00:52:54.040 --> 00:52:54.600
Toot it.
夸吧。

1229
00:52:55.860 --> 00:52:58.320
Well, Michael is going to confront Daryl.
迈克尔要去和达里尔对质了。

1230
00:52:58.480 --> 00:53:00.580
He says the chain of command is crumbling.
他说指挥链正在崩溃。

1231
00:53:00.580 --> 00:53:02.360
He just made Kevin cry.
他刚刚把凯文弄哭了。

1232
00:53:03.160 --> 00:53:03.360
Yeah.
是啊。

1233
00:53:03.880 --> 00:53:05.900
And Daryl says, I'm sorry you're upset.
达里尔说，很抱歉让你难过了。

1234
00:53:06.380 --> 00:53:09.600
And then Michael is like, well, thank you for your apology.
然后迈克尔就说，好吧，谢谢你的道歉。

1235
00:53:09.600 --> 00:53:11.800
I'd like this apology in front of everyone.
我希望你在大家面前道歉。

1236
00:53:12.040 --> 00:53:14.500
And Daryl says, I'm not apologizing to you.
达里尔说，我才不会向你道歉。

1237
00:53:14.680 --> 00:53:16.440
Yeah, he's like, you made a bad call.
是啊，他说，你做了一个错误的决定。

1238
00:53:16.660 --> 00:53:17.100
Yeah.
是啊。

1239
00:53:17.320 --> 00:53:18.380
And I fixed it.
而我把它修正了。

1240
00:53:18.980 --> 00:53:23.560
There is a line in this scene that I thought could go on a Halloween mug.
这一幕里有一句台词，我觉得可以印在万圣节马克杯上。

1241
00:53:23.980 --> 00:53:25.900
You tell me if you like it, Angela.
安吉拉，你告诉我你喜不喜欢。

1242
00:53:26.160 --> 00:53:26.400
Okay.
好的。

1243
00:53:26.700 --> 00:53:28.260
It's a Michael Scott quote.
这是迈克尔·斯科特的一句名言。

1244
00:53:28.260 --> 00:53:32.900
Quote, Halloween should be a day in which we honor monsters and not be mad at each other.
引用：万圣节应该是我们纪念怪物而不是互相生气的日子。

1245
00:53:33.720 --> 00:53:34.680
That's a good one.
那句不错。

1246
00:53:34.900 --> 00:53:35.220
Right?
对吧？

1247
00:53:35.440 --> 00:53:37.600
And then it has like little monster people on it.
上面还可以印些小怪物图案。

1248
00:53:37.740 --> 00:53:38.080
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1249
00:53:38.440 --> 00:53:40.800
Little Frankenstein and a mummy and everything.
小弗兰肯斯坦、木乃伊之类的。

1250
00:53:41.120 --> 00:53:41.260
Mm-hmm.
